    "turn_text": "I'm Michael Pope, and this is Pod Virginia Podcast that is enjoying the great outdoors today. We're about to head out to a Virginia nature triathlon with a man who set out to walk, ride, and paddle across the Commonwealth. He has a new book out next week about his journey. He's one of the few people on the planet who can actually claim the title, His Excellency, but on the Appalachian Trail, they call him Dog Bowl. Senator Tim Cain, thanks for joining us. Michael, I can't wait to talk to you about my journey. Good to be with you. Great. Well, so the title of your new book is Walk, Ride, Paddle, a Life outside, which is published by Harper Horizon. Now, ostensibly, the idea is pretty simple. You would hike the Appalachian Trail, cycle skyline drive, and paddle the James River, then journal about your experience. But that's only part of the story, because along the way, you share your thoughts about your first statewide campaign running for Lieutenant Governor, your approach to the harmonica, your thoughts about Jesus, your worries about being a good father, and what it's like campaigning on the national stage with Hillary Clinton. Tim Kane, why did you write this book?",
