    "turn_text": "Bowl. So on the trail, it's kind of a democratizing thing. You know, you're wearing the same clothes day after day. You're not shaving. You don't smell very good. And you use a trail name rather than your actual name. And the tradition on the trail is you have to be given the name. You can't choose the name. So for the first few weeks I was doing this on the trail, I would introduce myself as TK. And, you know, again, every once in a while somebody would recognize me. Most often they wouldn't, again, in hike and close, not shaving for a while. But I had a hack that I thought was great. I carried a collapsible dog bowl with me that every time I'd get to a stream, I'd fill that up. That would be a sink that I could use to wash my face or wash some socks out or something like that. And somebody who hiked with me a couple days saw it, and then the first day I thought it was a cool hack. And then the second day thought I was a little too proud of something that was somewhat obvious and just bestowed upon me the name Dog Bowl. And so from that point everywhere I went, I just introduced myself as Dog Bowl. And my dog had passed away. Gina, our life, our family dog had died not long before the hike. And her dog bowl was still sitting on the floor next to the kitchen table as a little reminder to us. That's not the ball I used on the trail. I brought my own dog bowl. Anyway, it just seemed like, yeah, that's a good nickname. So I stuck with it.",
