    "turn_text": "is ostensibly about a motorcycle journey from Minnesota to California along the way the author talks about everything from epistemology to the history of philosophy to the semantics of science. It also kind of reminded me of the quirky habit of journaling that was the hallmark of former Florida Senator Bob Graham. who was also a governor and found himself in the Senate and he would journal things like how long it took to rewind a VHS tape, that sort of thing. There's also, of course, hints of Henry David Thoreau and Life on the Woods. Senator Kane, what were your influences for this book and where do you see it fitting into the canon of American nonfiction? I",
