    "turn_text": "right across the street. And I'm just saying hi to voters, and I'm getting ready to go over to the university to do a talk to a student group. But all of a sudden, when you're on a national ticket, you have a press entourage. And they're usually kind of bored by it because they've heard you give the same speech, you know, five times. So they're around. But all of a sudden, they just clumped around me and it's like, oh, something's up. And they told me, Director Comey has reopened the investigation in Hillary Clinton's emails. This was the Friday, two Fridays before the elections, about 10 days before. And we could just watch the polling, particularly in the Pennsylvania, Wisconsin mission. We could just watch the polling dwindle, dwindle, dwindle because the email story was the head story for the next 10 days. It was the Sunday night before the election. I'm in Green Bay, Wisconsin. I'm doing an event at the University of Wisconsin, Green Bay. My press clumps around me again and they says, Director Comey has said they've done the investigation and no, there's no problem. There was nothing new, no challenging there. But I just had this sinking feeling, yeah, but a lot of damage has been done. You know, he made a miscalculation. There were two rules that were rules that had been established for a good reason by the Department of Justice and the FBI, which is you don't talk about a pending investigation. And you also don't inject controversy right before an election. There was a pending investigation into Donald Trump. Director Comey did not talk about that. and he did not inject controversy right before the election with respect to Donald Trump. He did talk about the Hillary Clinton email story and that injected controversy. So there was a set of two rules. He followed the rules with respect to one candidate and not the other. And look, there's a million factors that lead to an outcome of a race, but we could definitely see the effect that this had on polling as it was the lead story for the last, essentially the last 10 days of the campaign.",
