    "turn_text": "Well, I try to drink a milkshake every five pages. There's a number of instances of going to a place where like Shang-R-Lai expected to find a milkshake machine and it was broken or busted or COVID had closed the place down. Yeah, you lose a lot of weight on the hike, particularly when I did the hike, the heart of it was in August with an unusually long recess in August of 29. And I did like a 13-day section and then a weekend off and maybe a nine-day section and lost 26 pounds in that stretch. And it was because heat records are being busted. It was over 90 every day and water was dried up. And that was really a challenge. I'd say of the challenges of the hike, the absence of water was the most significant. And also you're working so hard, you'd think you would be just super hungry, but in some ways it's so hot. that, you know, almost sometimes the thought of eating made me nauseous. So yeah, I lost 26 pounds in that August stretch. Now it came back on pretty quickly once I got back to the sedentary United States Senate, but it was that the heat and the water were the real. the things that really made you struggle. And then as I talk about in the hiking section, there's a lot of things to be afraid of. The most fearsome thing is the smallest thing, which is ticks. And I had good",
