    "turn_text": "And we had a number of, look, my kids were with me on some of the journey. My friends' kids who had often done camping with us before were there. and and we did some imparting of wisdom but also I mean I gotta say it worked in reverse one of the stretches on the river I'm going along it's not with Adam it's his brother Jason who is a public high school teacher and my wife Anne is in the boat with me and Adam is in the boat with his dad and My wife Ann is a big educator on the State Board of Education, and we asked Adam, well, what's it like to be a high school teacher now? He's a late 20-something. So tell us about being a high school teacher, but tell us about your high school students. He had taught in an inner city, middle school in San Diego, and now he's at a public high school. in Hanover and New Hampshire near Dartmouth, both public schools, but kind of at the opposite end in terms of like, you know, wealth and demographic and social class of the students. And we had a fascinating discussion with him where he was talking about his work as a teacher, but also really sharing the stresses and challenges in kids' lives these days, the things that were completely similar about his San Diego and Dartmouth kids and the things that were completely different for them.",
